  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Bond order&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Number of electrons in bonding molecular orbitals.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mo>&#183;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo></math>&nbsp;Number of electrons in anti bonding molecular orbitals.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>&nbsp;has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>14</mn></math>&nbsp;electrons, it is isoelectronic with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;where Bond order&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>&nbsp;has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn></math>&nbsp;electrons&nbsp;is isoelectronic with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;whose bond order&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>&nbsp;has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>18</mn></math>&nbsp;electrons&nbsp;and&nbsp;is isoelectronic with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;whose bond order&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>So, the correct order of Bond order&nbsp;is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&#62;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>&#62;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>2</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math>.</p>",
